      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(ax^3+bx^2+\\cdots=0,\\) the sum of the roots is \\(-\\frac{b}{a}.\\) Here it is \\[ -\\frac{-8}{4}=2. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use Vieta’s formula for the sum of the roots of a cubic",
